<article class="env-definition" id="06KM">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/06KM">Definition <span data-tag="06KM">90.27.1</span>.</a> Let $(U, R, s, t, c)$ be a smooth prorepresentable groupoid in functors on $\mathcal{C}_\Lambda $. </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
We say $(U, R, s, t, c)$ is <em>normalized</em> if the groupoid $(U(k[\epsilon ]), R(k[\epsilon ]), s, t, c)$ is totally disconnected, i.e., there are no morphisms between distinct objects. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
We say $(U, R, s, t, c)$ is <em>minimal</em> if the $U \to [U/R]$ is given by a minimal versal formal object of $[U/R]$. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article>